Package: libreac6
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Roland REAC protocol library
 libreac speaks Roland REAC, the protocol between Roland digital consoles and
 their stageboxes, so a Linux machine can sit on a REAC network as an equal:
 hear a stagebox, enrol it, and read what it is straight from its own frames,
 its inputs and outputs, its model, its firmware.
 .
 It recognises a REAC frame, reads its sequence counter, detects the sample
 rate, and decodes and encodes the 24-bit audio in both directions. It also
 implements the REAC control plane: control blocks, head-amp records, box
 identity, and the master and slave establishment state machines.

Package: libreac-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libreac6 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Roland REAC protocol library, development files
 Headers and the pkg-config file for building programs against libreac, such
 as a REAC endpoint for a sound server.

Package: libreac-transport7
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Roland REAC transport layer
 libreac-transport carries the REAC protocol of libreac over the network:
 AF_PACKET frame receive and send over a lock-free ring, a real-time cadence
 pacer with clock discipline, network interface and VLAN scanning, segment
 locking, and the slave and master establishment built on libreac's state
 machines.
 .
 The library holds no Linux capability itself; that belongs to the program
 that uses it.

Package: libreac-transport-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libreac-transport7 (= ${binary:Version}), libreac-dev (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Roland REAC transport layer, development files
 Headers and the pkg-config file for building programs against libreac-
 transport.
